> integrate x^2 sin(x) from 0 to pi
∫ x^2*sin(x) dx
  = 2x*sin(x) + 2cos(x) - x^2*cos(x) + C
  check: d/dx of it equals the integrand at 401 points of [0, 3.14159] (max difference 8.9e-16)
  from 0 to 3.14159: F(3.14159) - F(0) = 5.86960440108936
  numeric (adaptive Gauss-Kronrod 7-15, 15 evaluations): 5.86960440108936, estimated error 6.5e-14
  the two agree to 0
> integrate exp(-x^2) from 0 to inf
∫ exp(-x^2) dx
  no antiderivative found (the rules here cover polynomials, powers and exp/sin/cos/tan/log of a linear argument, times a polynomial)
  numeric (adaptive Gauss-Kronrod 7-15, 105 evaluations): 0.886226925452757, estimated error 1.1e-14
> integrate 1/x from 1 to e
∫ 1/x dx
  = log(abs(x)) + C
  check: d/dx of it equals the integrand at 401 points of [1, 2.71828] (max difference 0)
  from 1 to 2.71828: F(2.71828) - F(1) = 1
  numeric (adaptive Gauss-Kronrod 7-15, 15 evaluations): 1, estimated error 1.1e-14
  the two agree to 0
> integrate x*exp(2x)
∫ x*exp(2x) dx
  = x/2*exp(2x) - 0.25exp(2x) + C
  check: d/dx of it equals the integrand at 401 points of [-10, 10] (max difference 6e-08)
> integrate 1/(2x + 1)^2 from 0 to 1
∫ 1/(2x + 1)^2 dx
  = -((2x + 1)^(-1)/2) + C
  check: d/dx of it equals the integrand at 401 points of [0, 1] (max difference 1.1e-16)
  from 0 to 1: F(1) - F(0) = 0.333333333333333
  numeric (adaptive Gauss-Kronrod 7-15, 15 evaluations): 0.333333333333343, estimated error 1.8e-14
  the two agree to 9.3e-15
> integrate tan(x) from 0 to 1
∫ tan(x) dx
  = -log(abs(cos(x))) + C
  check: d/dx of it equals the integrand at 401 points of [0, 1] (max difference 2.2e-16)
  from 0 to 1: F(1) - F(0) = 0.615626470386014
  numeric (adaptive Gauss-Kronrod 7-15, 15 evaluations): 0.615626470386014, estimated error 6.8e-15
  the two agree to 2.2e-16
> integrate 1/x from -1 to 1
∫ 1/x dx
  = log(abs(x)) + C
  check: d/dx of it equals the integrand at 400 points of [-1, 1] (max difference 0)
  numeric: the integrand is undefined or infinite inside the interval (singular or divergent)
